2. Find the **maximum area triangle** among all triangles formed by these points
3. Construct a **containing triangle** by drawing lines through each vertex parallel to the opposite side
4. **Reorder vectors into three chains** corresponding to the sides of this triangle, forming a closed path within it
5. Every triangle has an angle ≤ 60°, so translating that vertex to A_0 confines all points within 60°
6. Lower bound: 3 equal vectors at 120° (equilateral triangle) requires exactly 60°

